candidate:
\begin{align*}
\text{Step 1: Understand the problem.} \\
Mary has 30 sheep in total. She milks half of them for 1 kg of milk each, and the other half for 2 kg of milk each daily.

\text{Step 2: Calculate the number of sheep in each group.} \\
\text{Half of 30 sheep is } \frac{30}{2} = 15 \text{ sheep.}

\text{Step 3: Calculate the milk from the first group (1 kg each).} \\
15 \text{ sheep} \times 1 \text{ kg/sheep} = 15 \text{ kg of milk.}

\text{Step 4: Calculate the milk from the second group (2 kg each).} \\
15 \text{ sheep} \times 2 \text{ kg/sheep} = 30 \text{ kg of milk.}

\text{Step 5: Add the milk from both groups.} \\
15 \text{ kg} + 30 \text{ kg} = 45 \text{ kg of milk.}

\text{Step 6: Provide the final answer.} \\
\boxed{45 \text{ kg}}
\end{align*}

